  "lead_analysis": [
    "Replacing only the optimizer takes 2.5k from ATE 0.344 m / scale 1.219 to 0.105 m / 1.076 (COLMAP 0.072 / 1.026), confirming that the legacy BA's convergence was the main cause of the visloc scale/shape error on this rig.",
    "Termination is faithful: with the control's Ceres options (function_tolerance 0, gradient_tolerance 1e-4 absolute) Ceres also runs global BA to the 50-iteration cap on these gradients; cost converges by ~10 iterations.",
    "Remaining gap (ATE 1.46x, RPE-10s 1.8x): documented deviations still in the loop — local-BA point policy (COLMAP pulls in observations from images outside the window as fixed-pose residuals and refines those points; the port keeps them constant), 6-point DLT instead of GP3P for generalized registration, no structure-less registration fallback.",
    "Next: exact ParameterizePoints/AddPointToProblem semantics, then C3 GP3P; and a 5k run with the native BA to check the scale collapse that the legacy mapper showed between 2.5k and 5k."
  ]
